title Caravan ladder fold L -- the largest fold this arc has taken, and the meter with no name in its window
prompt Pick up the running thread Lindy-first crux-first, close open agent-closable reds first, take the next agent-doable lap, condense REMEMBER and refill its Now, send each finished increment.
think Standfast first. Read the living rows of crux/REDS.md and found every one carrying a closure -- %81, %83's booked prevention, %84, %98, %101, %102 -- with rows 1 through 100 folded to archive/ under the living-pin bound. No open agent-closable red stands, so the corrective queue is clear and the constructive one opens.
think The newest three log recommends all point one way, and fold K's names the crux outright: stand_taking_and_returning_reach standing in 42 of its 44 rungs under one hash, 1,435 lines carried, larger than any single fold this arc has taken. That is Lindy-first (the ladder is the durable surface) and crux-first (the hardest solvable move that opens the rest).
think Measured before trusting, as every fold here has. Extracted all 44 bodies and hashed them, and the card's own estimate came out conservative: 42 of 44 stand BYTE FOR BYTE at forty-four lines apiece, one hash, no mask needed at all. reclaim and revoke keep their own at 85 and 88 lines, their own content rather than a variation. So the fold is fold B's shape -- a check body lifting whole -- at the largest scale this ladder has offered.
think Verified the reach before a line moved, which is the check that has made every fold in this arc safe. Seven symbols the body names: offered, falling_promised, and Words already stood pub on all forty-two, nine folds of the publish-when-you-write-it habit compounding. Four wanted widening by one word each -- read_own_line, graft_promised_reach, return_promised_reach, reachable_between -- and four rungs that had never needed the harness wanted its import.
think Captured parity before the edit rather than after: built all 42 rungs and ran each, saving both the raw output and its sort. Then lifted the body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye reaching every helper through the rung handed in, left each rung a nine-line delegate, and captured the same 42 again.
think The proof came out the strongest this arc has shown. Every one of the forty-two sorted multisets stands identical with zero lines differing. Thirty-three rungs differ in ordered comparison by two to eighteen lines, and an unchanged binary run twice against itself differs by eight the same way -- so the interleave is the run rather than the fold, exactly as folds I, J, and K each proved before it.
think Then the part that outweighs the fold. Fold L was found by hand, by asking one wider question after six folds inside the tell_ family. That question deserved to become a meter rather than stay luck, so I asked it of every top-level body in every module and the answer reframes the whole arc.
think Three meters stood on this ladder and every one reads through a NAMED WINDOW -- check_, tell_, and one named function. Each is honest inside it and each says so in its own first sentence. What none can see is a body named anything else, which is precisely why the largest carry on the ladder rode free past all three for six consecutive folds. The answer is never a fourth named window; it is one window with no name in it.
think Built that meter. It reads every top-level body, compares by exact text rather than by hash so there is no collision to argue about, and prints the fold queue largest-first in half a second -- cheap enough for every lap, which is REDS %101's lesson about a question riding on the cost of its answer.
think Registered it in the choir on the lap it was born, which is the same REDS %101 lesson stated the other way, and the choir now sings 99 rather than 98.
obs The number is two orders of magnitude past the windows beside it. Checks carry 47, printing carries 2,686, the spine carries 0 -- and the whole ladder carries 142,850 lines across 10,198 copied bodies of the 17,975 standing in 102 modules. 698 families carry at least one copy and 247 carry past a hundred lines each. Every one of the three smaller numbers is true; none of them is the ladder's carry.
obs The largest family is mend_the_plan -- 36 rungs holding one 178-line body byte for byte, 6,230 carried, larger than any fold this arc has taken including this one. The fold queue now outlasts many laps, so no lap need guess what is next.
obs graft_promised_reach, one of the four helpers this lap widened to pub, stands in that queue at 1,763 carried across 42 rungs. A fold's own widening puts the next fold in view -- the habit compounding in a form I had not seen before.
obs A ratchet rather than a red against the three elder meters. Each named its window plainly in its own first sentence, so nothing was measured wrong; something was never measured. Yet the correction wants saying without softening: the arc's record had come to read the printing carry as THE carry, and it is a fiftieth of it. That is REDS %102's family at ladder scale, twice in two laps, and it is the reason the fourth meter is the durable half of this round rather than the fold.
obs The rota doc this lap was `foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md`, and it reads as though written for the round. Its teaching -- compress by making things publicly similar, grow the language in the canon rather than the syntax, and when compression cannot be had without magic keep the lines and keep the honesty -- is exactly what the comptime harness does. One public body reached through one word, `rung`. No macro, no private dialect, and a line removed by sameness is free forever.
obs The two rows a lift could most easily have inflated stood still for the eighth fold running: the byte-identical check carry at 47 and the orchestration spine at 0. A cost removed rather than traded, eight laps in a row.
